# Sky whale body plan — "LEVIATHAN", the scarred elder of the sky.
# A candidate body plan; preview it without booting the game:
#
#   godot --headless --path . --script tools/ship_preview.gd -- ships/whale_leviathan.ship
#
# The longest whale of the set. Vertical thickness is capped at 4 rows
# (owner survey 2026-08-20: thickest ~20-30 source blocks), so the
# elder's enormity is carried entirely by LENGTH — 38 authored columns
# against the reference's 24. Same sperm-whale reading: blunt head to
# the RIGHT, peduncle tapering to a fluke on the LEFT.
#
# The outline is weathered on purpose. The fluke's upper lobe is bitten
# clean off (leftmost column runs three rows, not four), and the dorsal
# ridge is chipped twice — a lone knuckle standing proud just ahead of
# the peduncle, then a two-cell notch gouged out of the back further
# forward. An elder does not keep a smooth line.
#
# TWO stomach cavities instead of the reference's one — this one has
# swallowed a lot. Both are 2-cell hollows fully enclosed by body on
# every orthogonal side: the forward one sits low (lower row, above
# the belly), the aft one sits high (upper row, under the back). Mine
# into either and you break through into a hollow.
#
#   W  blubber (buoyant flesh — keep it the majority or the whale falls)
#   M  meat (dense core)
#
# The whale floats because it is mostly blubber (here ~72%). Meat is a
# strict inner core: every meat cell has blubber or a stomach wall
# between it and the sky. Keep it one connected piece.

origin 20 1

..W........W.WWWW..WWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWW..
.WWWWWWWWWWWWWMMMWWM..MMMMMMMMMMMMMWWWW.
.WWWWWWWWWWWWWMMMMMMMMMMMM..MMMMMMMWWWW.
.WW.......WWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWW..
